 "text": "-->\nFS Grain - Homepage\n-->\nHomepage\nToggle Navigation\nCash Bids\nFutures\nAbout Us\nCareers\nCustomer Portal\nHome\nCash Bids\nCash Bids List\nCash Bids Grid\nUSDA Cash Bids\nMarket Data\nMarket Overview\nFutures\nOptions\nCustom Charts\nSpread Charts\nMarket Heat Maps\nStocks\nNews & Commentary\nAg Market Commentary\nInside Futures\nWeather\nLocal Weather\nNOAA Weather\nSign up for Alerts\nResources\nTrading Calendar\nFutures 101\nCommodity Symbols\nFarmer's Almanac\nUSDA Reports\nLocations\nSafety Data Sheets\nContact Us\nContact Your Merchandiser\nContact Your Originator\n-->\nPrevious\nNext\n-->\n-->\nCASH BIDS\n|\nHARVEST HOURS\n|\nFUTURES\n|\nLOCATIONS\n|\nGRAIN MARKETING\n|\nCUSTOMER PORTAL\n|\n|\nCASH BIDS\n|\n|\nHARVEST HOURS\n|\n|\nFUTURES\n|\n|\nLOCATIONS\n|\n|\nGRAIN MARKETING\n|\n|\nHARVEST HOURS\n|\n|\nCUSTOMER PORTAL\n|\n-->\nLocal Weather\nCheck your local Weather\n-->\nForecast\nDetailed Weather\nCattle Rally into the Weekend, as Cash Firms - October 16, 2026\nLive cattle futures caught some strength on Friday, with contracts up $1.10 to $1.65 at the close. December was up $1.30 on the week. USDA reported northern dressed sales at $350-355 and $222-227 live. Southern sales were reported at $228. The Friday morning Fed Cattle Exchange online auction showed sales...\nWheat Weakness Extends into the Weekend - October 16, 2026\nThe wheat complex headed into the weekend holding onto the weakness on Friday. Chicago SRW contracts fell lower on Friday, with contracts down 1 ½ to 9 ½ cents on the day and December losing 10 ½ cents this week. KC HRW futures slipped back 3 to 9 cents at...\nHog Bulls Find Footing on Friday, as Pork Sees Strength - October 16, 2026\nLean hog futures found some strength to close the week, with contracts up 27 cents to $1.25 on Friday. December was still down 90 cents for the week. USDA’s national base hog price was reported at $67.09 on Friday afternoon down $4.61 from the day prior. The CME Lean Hog...\nCotton Closes the Week with Mixed Trade - October 16, 2026\nCotton futures posted mixed trade on Friday, with contracts down 19 points to 24 points higher. December was down 54 points on the week. Crude oil was up $3.87 per barrel on the session, with the US dollar index $0.255 lower. Weekly CTC data showed managed money adding 1,862 contracts...\nSoybeans Slip Lower into the Weekend as Export Buying Continues - October 16, 2026\nSoybeans pulled off early losses on Friday, as contracts were down 1 ¾ to 3 cents in the front month and up ½ to 1 ¾ cents in the deferreds. November was 30 ¾ cents lower for the week. We are over halfway through October, as the average close for...\nCorn Falls on Friday as Spec Longs Continue Exit - October 16, 2026\nCorn futures closed out the Friday session with contracts 1 to 4 ½ cents across the board, as December was 5 ½ cents lower. The CmdtyView national average Cash Corn price was down 3 3/4 cents at $4.35. Now halfway through October the average close for December futures has been...\nFull Commentary...\nFS GRAIN Biometric Information Consent Form\nCustom Quotes\nName | Month | Last | Change | High | Low |\nCorn | Dec 26 | 474-2s | -3-6 | 481-0 | 473-0 |\nCorn | Mar 27 | 486-4s | -4-4 | 493-0 | 485-2 |\nCorn | May 27 | 493-4s | -4-4 | 499-6 | 492-4 |\nCorn | Jul 27 | 499-2s | -4-2 | 504-6 | 497-6 |\nCorn | Sep 27 | 494-0s | -3-4 | 498-4 | 492-2 |\nCorn | Dec 27 | 506-6s | -2-4 | 510-4 | 504-4 |\n|\nSoybean | Nov 26 | 1261-2s | -1-6 | 1265-6 | 1253-2 |\nSoybean | Jan 27 | 1275-6s | -2-0 | 1280-6 | 1268-4 |\nSoybean | Mar 27 | 1284-2s | -2-0 | 1289-2 | 1277-6 |\nSoybean | May 27 | 1292-2s | -2-6 | 1297-6 | 1286-4 |\nSoybean | Jul 27 | 1298-0s | -3-0 | 1303-4 | 1292-4 |\nSoybean | Aug 27 | 1282-2s | -2-6 | 1287-0 | 1277-0 |\nSoybean | Sep 27 | 1250-4s | +0-4 | 1251-6 | 1244-0 |\nSoybean | Nov 27 | 1240-6s | +1-6 | 1242-0 | 1233-2 |\n|\nWheat | Dec 26 | 660-4s | -9-4 | 670-2 | 656-2 |\nWheat | Mar 27 | 675-0s | -9-2 | 684-4 | 671-0 |\nWheat |